Key observations for downstream judgment (step 4+):
- All three top anomalies are in the **same region (E) and same month (2025-03)** across all three product lines — a synchronized spike, which is a classic channel-stuffing signature (a single regional push hitting every product line at once) rather than organic demand (which would typically be product-specific and region-specific).
- **E × Hardware** has an elevated return rate of **17.37%** in the spike month — high returns on a volume spike strongly suggest pushed inventory being returned, further supporting the channel-stuffing hypothesis.
- **E × Service** has a very low return rate (0.74%) — services are harder to "stuff" physically, so its spike may reflect a different mechanism (e.g., bundled promotions).
